    'न स्वतो नापि परतो न द्वाभ्यां नाप्यहेतुतः ।\nउत्पन्ना जातु विद्यन्ते भावाः क्वचन केचन ॥१॥\nचत्वारः प्रत्ययाः हेतुश्चालम्बनमनन्तरम् ।\nअधिपतेयं च तथा प्रत्ययो नास्ति पञ्चमः ॥२॥',
    'Chapter 1: Examination of Conditions\n\n1. Neither from itself, nor from another, nor from both, nor without a cause does any existing thing arise anywhere at all.\n\n2. There are four conditions: the efficient condition, the object-condition, the immediately preceding condition, and the dominant condition. There is no fifth condition.\n\n3. The essence of entities is not present in conditions. If the essence is not present, neither is the otherness present.\n\n4. Activity does not possess conditions; nor does it not possess conditions. Conditions do not possess activity; nor do they not possess it.',
