    'Chapter 1: Twin Verses (Yamaka-vagga)\n\n1. Mind is the forerunner of all actions. Mind is their chief; they are all mind-made. If one speaks or acts with a corrupt mind, suffering follows, as the wheel follows the hoof of the ox.\n\n2. Mind is the forerunner of all actions. Mind is their chief; they are all mind-made. If one speaks or acts with a pure mind, happiness follows, like a shadow that never departs.\n\n3. "He abused me, he struck me, he defeated me, he robbed me" — in those who harbor such thoughts, hatred will never cease.',
